--- stdout
This will tear down app "shop" on https://cp.example: every hosted environment is deleted.
  ENV       ID         DEPLOYMENTS   CUSTOM DOMAINS
  prod      env_prod   2             none
  staging   env_stg    2             none

Removed: each environment, its deployments, workloads, URLs, Flux objects, custom resources, namespaces
  AND its managed databases' data. IRREVERSIBLE (pass --keep-data to retain the databases).
Kept: the app — its name, release history and release images (not billed) — so
  `forge env deploy <env> <release>` recreates an env; custom domains stay in your organization, unbound.
Each env's secrets stop being delivered and are not given back to a recreated env: set them again.
Afterwards nothing runs or bills.

  prod     deleted; the platform is tearing it down
  staging  NOT deleted: only an org owner or admin may delete an environment
--- error
deleted 1 of 2 envs of app "shop"; not deleted: staging
fix: each refusal is printed above (tearing down an app needs an org owner or admin); resolve it and re-run `forge app teardown`, which deletes only the envs that remain
